    {
      "id": "f-indexed-handle-manager-base",
      "name": "FIndexedHandleManagerBase",
      "category": "IndexedHandle",
      "signature": "FIndexedHandleManagerBase()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Handle Manager meant for FIndexedHandleBase and FCompactIndexedHandleBase derived classes, handles are given out from a freelist and are zero based and consecutive in nature,\nso ideal for being used as indices in to arrays.\nUsing bOptimizeHandleReuse performance impact on releasing a handle. Because new handles will always use the smallest index, this will help greatly the compaction code(ShrinkHandles) and reduce the total number of handles.\nThis is very useful when you need to iterate through every valid handles often."
    },
